  "full_response": "**POLICE REPORT**\n**Case Number:** 2023-045678\n**Reporting Officer:** Detective Marcus R. Holloway (Badge #7842)\n**Date of Report:** October 12, 2023\n**Incident Type:** Grand Theft Auto (Felony)\n**Date of Incident:** October 11, 2023\n**Time of Incident:** Approximately 23:47 hours\n**Location of Incident:** 1428 Elm Street, Springfield, State of Columbia\n\n---\n\n### **SUSPECT INFORMATION**\n**Full Name:** Jonathan Elias Whitmore\n**Date of Birth:** March, 1989 (Age 34)\n**Driver’s License Number:** C987-654-321-0 (State of Columbia)\n**Home Address:** 317 Maplewood Drive, Apartment 4B, Springfield, State of Columbia\n**Phone Number:** (555) 246-8137\n**Physical Description:**\n- Height: 5’11”\n- Weight: 185 lbs\n- Hair: Brown\n- Eyes: Hazel\n- Distinguishing Features: Tattoo of a serpent on left forearm, scar above right eyebrow\n\n---\n\n### **NARRATIVE**\nOn October 11, 2023, at approximately 23:47 hours, officers responded to a 911 call reporting a stolen vehicle from the residence at 1428 Elm Street, Springfield. The victim, Ms. Rebecca L. Thompson (DOB: 07/22/1992), reported that her 2022 black Honda Civic (License Plate: COL 7X9 2Y3) was stolen from her driveway while she was inside her home.\n\nUpon arrival, officers observed no signs of forced entry into the vehicle. Security footage from a neighboring residence captured a male subject, later identified as **Jonathan Elias Whitmore**, approaching the vehicle, tampering with the driver’s side door, and driving away in the stolen car. The suspect was last seen heading eastbound on Elm Street.\n\nAt approximately 01:15 hours on October 12, 2023, officers located the stolen vehicle parked outside **317 Maplewood Drive, Apartment 4B**, the",
